      "IssueType": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "Priority": {
        "description": "Issue priority (spine §1.2): a transparent newtype over `i32`, valid range `0..=4`.\n\nOrdering is numeric, so `CRITICAL < HIGH < MEDIUM < LOW < BACKLOG` — this is the order the\nhybrid ready-sort relies on. `Default` is [`Priority::MEDIUM`]. The wire form is the bare\ninteger (`#[serde(transparent)]`), and `Display` renders `\"P{n}\"`.\n\n# Examples\n\n```\nuse unblock_model::Priority;\nuse std::str::FromStr;\n\nassert_eq!(Priority::default(), Priority::MEDIUM);\nassert_eq!(Priority::CRITICAL.to_string(), \"P0\");\nassert_eq!(Priority::from_str(\"p1\").unwrap(), Priority::HIGH);\nassert!(Priority::from_str(\"P5\").is_err());\nassert!(Priority::CRITICAL < Priority::BACKLOG);\n```",
        "format": "int32",
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "Status": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "description": "The `issue` tool input (spine §5.2 — EXACT shape; 7 actions).",
    "oneOf": [
      {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/CreateInput",
        "description": "Create a new issue (interactive MINTING create, D21).\n\nThe payload is boxed (it is the largest variant) — the wire shape is unchanged: a newtype\nvariant over a `#[serde(flatten)]`-equivalent struct keeps `{action:\"create\", title, ...}`.",
        "properties": {
          "action": {
            "const": "create",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "action"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      {
        "description": "Bulk-create issues from an inline markdown document (D22 — `{action:\"create_bulk\", markdown}`).\n\nThe `markdown` is INLINE content (NOT a path). The adapter parses it (all-or-nothing\npre-mutation), caps the record count at `Quotas::max_batch`, maps each `ParsedIssue` →\n`NewIssue` (carrying the symbolic dep/parent refs verbatim), and calls the ATOMIC\n`Session::create_bulk` — NOT a loop over `create_issue`. The engine mints all ids + resolves the\n2-phase intra-file dep/parent IN MEMORY + inserts the whole batch in ONE tx (rollback-on-any-\nfailure → ZERO writes). Output reuses `ToolOutput::Issues`.",
        "properties": {
          "action": {
            "const": "create_bulk",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "markdown": {
            "description": "The inline bulk-markdown document content.",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "action",
          "markdown"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
